  {
    "sha": "179ef8a3f44c9b1a1b93c3491e121edd81d23f5d",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDE3OWVmOGEzZjQ0YzliMWExYjkzYzM0OTFlMTIxZWRkODFkMjNmNWQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T09:50:53Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T09:50:53Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): \"Wireframe, see-through\" display mode\n\nThe Display menu has a fifth display mode. It draws each edge of the\nmodel and of the stock, front and back, and no face: not to the color\nbuffer and not to the depth buffer. The model hides nothing behind it.\n\nA click in the mode picks hidden edges too, by the existing rule of\n`pick_bodies`: nearest to the cursor first, then nearest to the camera.\nThe toolbar's wireframe switch treats the mode as a wireframe. The view\nfile stores the mode as `wireframe-see-through`.\n\nStacked on #2835 (#2818), which adds \"Shaded\" without edges, the draw\nlist and the saved display mode.\n\nFixes #2636\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
